course: dictionary
lesson: 14228
title: Narration
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Narration is the telling of a story. The person who tells the story is the narrator. In a film, show or play, narration can also be the spoken words that explain what is happening.
explain: First-person narration uses I or we, so the narrator is part of the story: «I climbed the tree and saw the sea.»
explain: Third-person narration uses he, she or they, so the narrator is outside the story and watches it: «She climbed the tree and saw the sea.»
explain: Documentaries often have a narration, a voice that tells you facts while you watch the pictures.
fact: Narration means the telling of a story, especially by a narrator.
fact: Narration can also mean the spoken words that explain what is happening in a film, show or play.
fact: First-person narration uses words like I and we.
fact: Third-person narration uses words like he, she and they.
fact: Documentaries have a narration.
exercise: In «I ran to the shop and bought bread.», which word shows first-person narration? | They | *I | He | The
exercise: A documentary about whales has a voice that explains what is on the screen. What is that voice called? | *Narration | A rhyme | A chorus | A title
exercise: «She walked home and waved at the dog.» Is this first-person or third-person narration? | Neither | *Third person | Both at once | First person
test: What does narration mean? | A kind of bread | *The telling of a story, especially by a narrator | To shout loudly | A small boat with one sail
test: Which sentence uses third-person narration? | *«They played football until the sun went down.» | «We played football until the sun went down.» | «I played football until the sun went down.»
exam: In «The film's narration explained how bees make honey.», what does narration mean? | A dance for the stage | A type of food | *The spoken words that explain what is happening | The end of a story
